# Line-ending policy: every text file is stored and checked out as LF.
# Explicit here because core.autocrlf varies by machine and silently
# rewrites endings - that variance is what kept triggering "LF will be
# replaced by CRLF" warnings. Windows batch files stay CRLF: cmd.exe can
# mis-parse LF-only .bat files.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.bat text eol=crlf
